<title>NETHERLANDS: Delta Lloyd Bank raises Gamma to Buy.</title>
<headline>Delta Lloyd Bank raises Gamma to Buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Feb 14 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Gamma	     textile	  99.00  Delta Lloyd Bank</p>
<p>COMMENT: BUY (Hold). The outlook for 1997 and 1998 is good. Modest organic growth completed with consolidation of recent acquisitions (U.S. Chemprene in December and a 50 percent stake in France's Delcar) will support profit growth. Management announced earlier that it expected a 20 percent profit increase for 1996. Gamma just started a central treasury desk. This will reduce the risk profile and support cost and tax reductions.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS		P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	6.18	     16.0     4.00</p>
<p>    1996		   7.88	     12.6     4.00</p>
<p>    1997		   9.07	     10.9     4.20</p>
<p>    1998		   9.75	     10.2     4.50</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
